<title>RUSSIA: Details of forthcoming major Russian privatisations.</title>
<headline>Details of forthcoming major Russian privatisations.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia plans to raise billions of dollars this year with sales of government stakes in a range of companies. Planned sales announced by privatisation officials still to take place this year include the following:</p>
<p> Company		   Industry    Stake	Value</p>
<p> NK LUKoil		  Oil	   15.00 pct  $1.5 billion*</p>
<p> NK LUKoil options			4.97 pct</p>
<p> AO Svyazinvest	  Telecoms    49 pct     N/A</p>
<p> RAO UES		   Power	1.5-2 pct $150-$200 million*</p>
<p>(Unified Energy System) utility</p>
<p> NGK Slavneft	    Oil	   19.68 pct  N/A</p>
<p> Rosgosstrakh	    Insurance   50 pct     N/A</p>
<p> OAO Nafta-Moskva	Oil trading 14.99 pct  $18.5 million**</p>
<p> AO Novoship	     Shipping     5.34 pct  N/A</p>
<p>* Reuter calculation as percentage of shareholders equity based on Wednesday midday share price on Russian Trading System ** Government-declared minimum bid price.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
